\subsection{QA2: Wikipedia QA Dataset}
This dataset contains three tasks on a large Wikipedia QA dataset.
\paragraph{Question-only Summary}
The task is to generate a question summary from a single question in the dataset. The questions are asked about Wikipedia articles with more than 300 words in them. The summaries of the questions are generated without any reference. 
\paragraph{Answer-only Summary}
The task is to generate a summary of an answer to a question, given the question and the answer.

\section{Conclusion}

In conclusion, we propose a novel model for generating an abstractive summary. Our model uses an attention mechanism in combination with a self-attention mechanism to produce an abstractive summary. Our model is evaluated using two metrics, ROUGE-L and BLEU, and is shown to be superior to several other state-of-the-art models, including the Bi-LSTM model and the Transformer model. 

